# =============================================================================
# DATASET SAFETY -- read this before touching this file.
#
# The PNG (Pulmonary Nodule Growth) dataset lives in data/external/png/. It
# is ~1,536 NIfTI volumes of patient data collected under a hospital ethics
# approval (see docs/datasets.md). It must NEVER be committed: it is not
# ours to redistribute. The *.nii / *.nii.gz rules below are what actually
# prevent this even if the folder location changes -- do not weaken them.
# This dataset is UNRELATED to the LDCT-IQAC dataset below; both datasets'
# rules coexist in this one file, but neither implies anything about the
# other (see docs/replication/dataset_adaptation.md).
# =============================================================================

# --- the PNG dataset: ignored in full ---
# Not just the volumes -- patient-characteristics.csv carries per-patient
# age/sex, characteristics.csv per-nodule measurements, and NGP3T.json the
# manifest tying them together. All of it is patient data.
data/external/

# --- LDCT-IQAC dataset: raw images ignored, JSON score labels kept ---
# data/raw/ldct_iqac/train/image/ and data/raw/ldct_iqac/test/images/ hold
# the LDCT-IQAC CT images themselves (TIFF, patient-derived) -- never
# commit these. They're covered by the generic `data/raw/**` rule below;
# the *.tif/*.tiff extension rules further down are the real backstop that
# survives any future path rename (this dataset's directories have already
# been renamed once -- see docs/repository_architecture_audit.md).
#
# data/labels/ldct_iqac/*.json contain only filename -> quality-score
# pairs (no pixel data) and are small/useful for reproducibility, so they
# are INTENTIONALLY NOT ignored by any rule in this file -- do not add a
# blanket `data/**` rule that would silently start ignoring them.

# --- derived and working data ---
data/raw/**
data/interim/**
data/processed/**
!data/**/
!data/**/.gitkeep
!data/README.md

# Other conventional dataset locations, kept even though unused today, in
# case this project or a fork of it grows one.
datasets/**
archive/**
!datasets/**/.gitkeep
!archive/**/.gitkeep

# --- medical-image and archive formats, wherever they appear ---
*.dcm
*.dicom
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.mhd
*.raw
*.tif
*.tiff
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.rar
*.gz

# --- pretrained weights (externally-sourced) and experiment checkpoints ---
# Pretrained weights (weights/pretrained/radimagenet/resnet50/*.h5, *.pt)
# and experiment-generated checkpoints (experiments/<NNN_name>/checkpoint/*.pt)
# are both binary model weights -- caught by the extension rules below
# (*.h5, *.pt, etc.) regardless of which of the two directories they're
# in. Deliberately NOT using a directory-level `weights/pretrained/**` or
# `experiments/**/checkpoint/**` rule here: git cannot un-ignore a file
# nested inside an ignored directory, which would make it impossible to
# keep each directory's README.md/.gitkeep tracked. Extension-based
# ignoring avoids that trap while still catching the binaries wherever
# they land (see docs/decisions/README.md, "Experiment checkpoints live
# under experiments/, not weights/").
*.ckpt
*.pth
*.pt
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pb
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.npy
*.npz
checkpoints/
outputs/

# --- generated evaluation outputs ---
# Figures/tables/predictions/metrics are regenerated by evaluation
# notebooks, not authored -- keep the directories (via .gitkeep) but not
# their generated contents. (`results/**` here is safe to negate into,
# unlike weights/experiments above, because only .gitkeep files are ever
# added back -- see the allow-list.)
results/**
!results/**/
!results/**/.gitkeep

# --- TensorBoard / training logs / caches ---
logs/
*.tfevents.*
.cache/

# =============================================================================
# EXPLICIT ALLOW-LIST -- small, intentionally-committed images stay committable.
# =============================================================================
!docs/**/*.jpg
!docs/**/*.png
!tests/fixtures/**

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.benchmarks/

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
